# Shackle Slinger: 3/2; flurry - "Whenever you cast your second spell each turn, choose target creature an opponent controls. If it's
# tapped, put a stun counter on it. Otherwise, tap it." Turn 1: Black Lotus, then the Slinger as the second spell (it is not yet on the
# battlefield: no trigger). Turn 3: Bot1's second spell (the second Ornithopter) taps Bot2's untapped Llanowar Elves, with no stun
# counter; the only legal target (never its own Slinger or Ornithopters: "an opponent controls") is chosen for it. Turn 4: Bot2 untaps and taps its
# Elves for mana. Turn 5: Bot1's second spell finds the Elves tapped, so it gets a stun counter instead (and stays tapped); the
# first spell of each turn did nothing.

